---
/*
 * Over mij — the person behind Leonard Rieksen Fotografie (P5 — D-31). Builds trust and personal context
 * (13.42/2.21) without becoming an autobiography (13.45): who Leo is, his background, his photographic
 * vision, his working approach, the human component — each beat justified by the trust/expertise/identity
 * test (13.45). Blueprint flow 13.46 (header · introductie · portret · achtergrond · visie · werkwijze ·
 * portfolio-koppeling · contact-CTA · footer) is honoured but consolidated into fewer, stronger beats.
 *
 * CONTENT AUTHORITY (CLAUDE §9.2): every factual claim here is TRANSFORMED from Leo's OWN published bio
 * (reference/old-website/over-mij.html) — his own words about his training, specialisation and approach.
 * This is migration/transformation of his self-description, NOT invention. Naming: "Leo Rieksen" for the
 * personal register (2.21/3.8.2). The two named specialisations stay Architectuur + Interieur (D-07);
 * vastgoed/avondfotografie are mentioned as factual parts of his background, not elevated to services.
 * Bio facts remain owner-confirm (A-02) — Leo's own site copy, not independently re-validated.
 *
 * ART DIRECTION (D-28/D-29/D-30 frozen grammar): this page carries the nocturne identity in its OWN
 * signature — a low-key studio portrait whose dark backdrop dissolves into the page (the figure emerges
 * from the nocturne rather than sitting in a hard frame), and a monumental VISIE statement that is the
 * page's premium non-photographic moment. Its genuine cross-boundary crossing is TYPOGRAPHIC (the vision
 * statement physically straddles the achtergrond→visie section seam) — deliberately a DIFFERENT mechanism
 * from the three existing photo-vertical-rise crossings (portfolio lead / diensten / interieur). Gold stays
 * a selective hairline/datum; photography (the portrait) is the dominant image.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Media from '../components/Media.astro';
import ContactCta from '../components/ContactCta.astro';
import portretImg from '../assets/static/overmij.jpeg';
import visieImg from '../assets/static/avond-deventer.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Over mij"
	description="Leo Rieksen — de fotograaf achter Leonard Rieksen Fotografie. Een rustige, precieze benadering van architectuur- en interieurfotografie, met een scherp oog voor licht, lijnen en sfeer."
>
	<!-- 1. HERO — editorial split (introductie + portret, 13.46). Deliberately NOT the full-bleed scrim hero
	     of the home/service pages: an eyebrow + name + lead against the low-key portrait, whose dark studio
	     backdrop dissolves into the page so Leo emerges from the nocturne. The portrait is this page's LCP
	     candidate (priority-loaded). -->
	<Section as="header" class="about-hero">
		<div class="about-hero__grid">
			<div class="about-hero__intro u-reveal">
				<p class="t-eyebrow t-eyebrow--accent" style="--reveal-index: 0">Over mij</p>
				<h1 class="t-display about-hero__name" style="--reveal-index: 1">Leo Rieksen</h1>
				<p class="t-lead about-hero__lead" style="--reveal-index: 2">
					Fotograaf met een rustige benadering en een scherp oog voor detail. Ik leg architectuur en
					interieur vast met aandacht voor licht, lijnen en sfeer — vaak in het bijzondere licht van het
					avond- en blauwe uur.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="about-hero__portrait u-inview">
				<Media
					src={portretImg}
					alt="Portret van fotograaf Leo Rieksen — grijzend haar en baard, rustige blik, in een donkere studio."
					priority={true}
					widths={[420, 640, 860]}
					sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 34vw, 80vw"
					ratio="4/5"
					position="center 34%"
					class="about-hero__media"
				/>
			</div>
		</div>
	</Section>

	<!-- 2. ACHTERGROND (professionele achtergrond, 13.44/13.46). Prose in Leo's own voice, transformed from
	     his bio. Reserves generous trailing space so the VISIE statement below can rise across the seam. -->
	<Section as="section" class="about-bg">
		<div class="about-bg__grid">
			<div class="about-bg__head">
				<p class="t-eyebrow t-eyebrow--accent">Achtergrond</p>
				<h2 class="t-h2 about-bg__title">Van jongs af gefascineerd door beeld.</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="about-bg__body prose">
				<p>
					Al vanaf mijn tiende jaar fascineert beeld mij: hoe licht, lijnen en sfeer samen een verhaal
					kunnen vormen. Die nieuwsgierigheid bracht mij via de eerste cursussen naar de Fotovakschool.
				</p>
				<p>
					Daarna volgde ik aanvullende opleidingen en verdiepte ik mij in boeken en in de technische
					ontwikkelingen binnen het vak. Mijn specialisatie ligt bij architectuur- en interieurfotografie
					— met daarnaast vastgoed — vaak aangevuld met avondfotografie.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</Section>

	<!-- 3. VISIE (visie op fotografie, 13.46). The page's premium NON-photographic moment AND its genuine
	     cross-boundary crossing: Leo's own defining line, set at display scale, physically STRADDLES the
	     achtergrond→visie section seam. A TYPOGRAPHIC crossing — a substantial content element crossing a
	     boundary between two visibly-distinct fields (base ink-900 above, a modelled deep field here) — a
	     deliberately different mechanism from the site's three photo-vertical-rise crossings (D-30/D-31). -->
	<Section as="section" class="about-visie">
		<div class="about-visie__inner">
			<div class="about-visie__marker">
				<span class="about-visie__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
				<p class="t-eyebrow t-eyebrow--accent about-visie__eyebrow">Visie</p>
			</div>
			<h2 class="t-display about-visie__statement">
				Ik hoor vaker dat mijn foto&rsquo;s mooier uitpakken dan de werkelijkheid.
			</h2>
			<p class="about-visie__support">
				Voor mij is dat het teken dat techniek en gevoel samenvallen — dat lange sluitertijden en
				zorgvuldige belichting precies de sfeer opleveren die een ruimte of gebouw verdient. Ik let op
				lijnen, op licht, en op alles wat kan afleiden van het beeld dat ik voor ogen heb.
			</p>
		</div>
		<!-- P5.1 (D-32) — a single atmospheric photograph fills the visie section's previously-empty right field
		     (owner: the space beside the vision statement read as too empty on desktop). Chosen by VISUAL inspection,
		     not filename: a long-exposure evening architecture frame (a church in Deventer) — warm-lit stone against a
		     deep blue night with moon-glow and drifting cloud — the literal illustration of the statement ("lange
		     sluitertijden en zorgvuldige belichting… de sfeer"; "mooier dan de werkelijkheid"). Architecture, so it
		     does NOT compete with the portrait hero; nocturne palette. Its dark sky edges melt into the deep field
		     via the same inward mask as the portrait (emerge-from-the-nocturne), so it reads as spatial depth, NOT a
		     pasted rectangle — and it COMPLEMENTS the typographic crossing: the statement still straddles the seam,
		     the photo stays anchored on the deep field (it does not cross), so the crossing mechanism is not duplicated. -->
		<figure class="about-visie__figure u-inview">
			<Media
				src={visieImg}
				alt="Een gotische kerk in Deventer bij avond — warm uitgelicht metselwerk en torenspitsen tegen een diepblauwe nachthemel met maanlicht."
				widths={[420, 640, 900]}
				sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 32vw, 82vw"
				ratio="4/5"
				position="center 30%"
				class="about-visie__media"
			/>
		</figure>
	</Section>

	<!-- 4. WERKWIJZE + persoonlijk + portfolio-koppeling (13.46). A first-person, reflective prose block —
	     deliberately NOT the third-person numbered 01/02/03 method used on the home/service pages, so Over
	     mij stays compositionally distinct. Closes with the human note and a route into the work. This area
	     is intentionally the RESTRAINED beat (no crossing, no added atmosphere) — calm before the CTA. -->
	<Section as="section" class="about-work">
		<div class="about-work__grid">
			<div class="about-work__head">
				<p class="t-eyebrow t-eyebrow--accent">Werkwijze</p>
				<h2 class="t-h2 about-work__title">Eerst luisteren, dan fotograferen.</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="about-work__body">
				<div class="prose">
					<p>
						Voor elke opdracht ga ik eerst in gesprek. Ik luister goed, inventariseer de wensen en vertaal
						die naar beelden die helder, rustig en krachtig zijn.
					</p>
					<p>
						Ik woon in Midden-Nederland, hou van sport en haal veel voldoening uit het moment waarop alles
						klopt: de sfeer, het licht en het beeld dat precies overbrengt wat bedoeld was. Als fotograaf
						wil ik een betrouwbare partner zijn — iemand die met aandacht en vakmanschap helpt om iets
						bijzonders vast te leggen.
					</p>
				</div>
				<p class="about-work__more">
					<a class="link-arrow" href="/portfolio/">
						Bekijk het werk
						<svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 12h15M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg>
					</a>
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</Section>

	<ContactCta
		heading="Samen iets bijzonders vastleggen?"
		text="Benieuwd wat ik voor uw project kan betekenen? Neem gerust vrijblijvend contact op — dan bespreken we kort wat u zoekt."
		primaryLabel="Neem contact op"
		primaryHref="/contact/"
		secondaryLabel="Bekijk het portfolio"
		secondaryHref="/portfolio/"
	/>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	/* ============================================================= *
	 * 1. HERO — editorial split; the portrait dissolves into the nocturne
	 * ============================================================= */
	.about-hero {
		position: relative;
		isolation: isolate;
		overflow-x: clip;
	}
	.about-hero__grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 0.95fr;
		gap: var(--space-2xl) clamp(var(--space-2xl), 1rem + 6vw, var(--space-4xl));
		align-items: center;
	}
	.about-hero__name {
		margin-top: var(--space-md);
		max-width: 12ch;
	}
	.about-hero__lead {
		margin-top: var(--space-lg);
		max-width: 42ch;
		color: var(--color-text);
	}
	.about-hero__portrait {
		position: relative;
	}
	/* The source is a low-key studio portrait on a dark, vignetted backdrop that already fades to near-black
	   at its edges. A soft inward mask on the inner (left) and lower edges lets the plate melt into the page
	   so the figure "escapes its field" instead of reading as a hard rectangle — a premium, portrait-specific
	   treatment (the nocturne surround IS the studio backdrop). Decorative only; the <img> carries the alt. */
	.about-hero__media {
		-webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(120% 108% at 68% 40%, #000 62%, transparent 100%);
		mask-image: radial-gradient(120% 108% at 68% 40%, #000 62%, transparent 100%);
	}
	@media (max-width: 60rem) {
		.about-hero__grid {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: var(--space-xl);
		}
		.about-hero__name {
			max-width: 16ch;
		}
		.about-hero__portrait {
			max-width: 24rem;
		}
	}

	/* ============================================================= *
	 * 2. ACHTERGROND — base-dark prose; reserves trailing space for the crossing
	 * ============================================================= */
	.about-bg__grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 0.9fr 1.1fr;
		gap: var(--space-2xl) clamp(var(--space-3xl), 2rem + 5vw, var(--space-4xl));
		align-items: start;
	}
	.about-bg__title {
		margin-top: var(--space-sm);
		max-width: 14ch;
	}
	.about-bg__body {
		max-width: var(--measure);
	}
	/* Reserve empty space at the foot so the VISIE statement below can rise into it without colliding with
	   this prose (the upper field of the typographic crossing). */
	.about-bg {
		padding-bottom: clamp(5rem, 3rem + 8vw, 11rem);
	}
	@media (max-width: 52rem) {
		.about-bg__grid {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: var(--space-lg);
		}
		.about-bg__title {
			max-width: 18ch;
		}
	}

	/* ============================================================= *
	 * 3. VISIE — the modelled deep field + the TYPOGRAPHIC boundary crossing (D-31)
	 * ============================================================= *
	 * This section is a deliberately DEEPER, modelled field than the ink-900 achtergrond above, so the two
	 * fields read as visibly distinct (the precondition for a true crossing, D-30). Its own background starts
	 * at the section box (the field seam is fixed there); the eyebrow + monumental statement lift via a single
	 * spacing-token negative margin so they RISE ACROSS that seam into the achtergrond's reserved space, while
	 * the support line settles below the seam on the deep field. The statement is a substantial content
	 * element straddling two distinct fields — a genuine crossing, delivered by TYPE (not a photo rising).
	 * Robust: additive negative margin only, painting-above is automatic (later DOM), disabled when stacked. */
	.about-visie {
		position: relative;
		isolation: isolate;
		overflow-x: clip;
		--cross-rise: clamp(2.5rem, 0.5rem + 6vw, 7rem);
		background:
			radial-gradient(
				96% 62% at 16% 14%,
				rgba(var(--p-atmos-cool), 0.14) 0%,
				rgba(var(--p-atmos-cool), 0.04) 44%,
				rgba(var(--p-atmos-cool), 0) 72%
			),
			linear-gradient(180deg, #0b0f17 0%, #070a10 54%, #090c14 100%);
	}
	/* Reduced top padding so the statement's negative margin lifts it ACROSS the seam into the achtergrond
	   field above (rather than merely trimming a large default padding) — the D-30 robust-crossing pattern.
	   Element+class selector (`section.about-visie`) so it reliably outweighs `.section`'s `padding-block`
	   regardless of CSS bundle source order (a plain `.about-visie` tie was order-dependent and fragile). */
	section.about-visie {
		padding-top: clamp(1.5rem, 0.5rem + 2vw, 3rem);
	}
	/* A faint deep frame top+foot so the statement sits in a modelled space, not a flat fill (premium
	   non-photographic zone — D-29 Limitation 4). aria-hidden decorative. */
	.about-visie::before {
		content: '';
		position: absolute;
		inset: 0;
		z-index: -1;
		pointer-events: none;
		background: linear-gradient(
			180deg,
			rgba(5, 7, 11, 0.55) 0%,
			rgba(5, 7, 11, 0) 26%,
			rgba(5, 7, 11, 0) 82%,
			rgba(5, 7, 11, 0.5) 100%
		);
	}
	/* Flex column so the inner's negative margin reliably lifts it (a plain block container would collapse
	   the negative top margin instead of crossing — the D-30 diensten crossing uses the same flex pattern). */
	/* P5.1 (D-32) — two-column grid: statement/text (left) + the atmospheric photograph (right). Grid (like flex)
	   does NOT collapse the inner's negative top margin, so the TYPOGRAPHIC crossing is fully preserved: the text
	   column still rises across the seam; the figure column is anchored on the deep field (align-items:start, no
	   lift) so it COMPLEMENTS the crossing rather than duplicating the photo-rise idiom. */
	.about-visie :global(.u-container) {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 0.78fr);
		gap: clamp(var(--space-2xl), 1rem + 5vw, var(--space-4xl));
		align-items: start;
	}
	.about-visie__figure {
		margin-top: clamp(0.5rem, -0.5rem + 3vw, 2.5rem);
	}
	/* The photo's dark night-sky edges melt into the deep field via the same inward mask as the portrait hero, so
	   it emerges from the nocturne rather than reading as a pasted rectangle. Decorative; the img carries the alt. */
	.about-visie__media {
		-webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(128% 122% at 52% 44%, #000 66%, transparent 100%);
		mask-image: radial-gradient(128% 122% at 52% 44%, #000 66%, transparent 100%);
	}
	.about-visie__inner {
		max-width: 54ch;
		/* Lift the eyebrow + statement across the section seam into the achtergrond field above. */
		margin-top: calc(-1 * var(--cross-rise));
	}
	.about-visie__marker {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: var(--space-md);
		margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
	}
	/* Short champagne datum rule (the selective gold precision idiom — 6.11/6.12, D-28 family), marking the
	   page's defining statement. Gold stays a hairline, never a fill. */
	.about-visie__rule {
		flex: none;
		width: clamp(2rem, 1.4rem + 2vw, 3.25rem);
		height: 1px;
		background: linear-gradient(
			90deg,
			rgba(199, 165, 106, 0) 0%,
			rgba(199, 165, 106, 0.5) 34%,
			rgba(224, 197, 140, 0.92) 100%
		);
	}
	.about-visie__statement {
		max-width: 22ch;
		font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 1.2rem + 3.4vw, 4rem);
	}
	.about-visie__support {
		margin-top: var(--space-xl);
		max-width: 52ch;
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
	}
	@media (max-width: 52rem) {
		/* The typographic crossing is a desktop composition move; on the single column restore normal spacing
		   so the statement doesn't ride up into the achtergrond prose. The photo stacks below the text (P5.1). */
		.about-visie :global(.u-container) {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: var(--space-xl);
		}
		.about-visie__inner {
			margin-top: 0;
			max-width: none;
		}
		.about-visie__figure {
			margin-top: 0;
			max-width: 26rem;
		}
	}

	/* ============================================================= *
	 * 4. WERKWIJZE + persoonlijk — the restrained beat (no crossing, no added atmosphere)
	 * ============================================================= */
	.about-work__grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 0.85fr 1.15fr;
		gap: var(--space-2xl) clamp(var(--space-3xl), 2rem + 5vw, var(--space-4xl));
		align-items: start;
	}
	.about-work__head {
		max-width: 26ch;
	}
	.about-work__title {
		margin-top: var(--space-sm);
	}
	.about-work__more {
		margin-top: var(--space-xl);
	}
	@media (max-width: 52rem) {
		.about-work__grid {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: var(--space-lg);
		}
	}
</style>
